=== Yanbaru wrestling stars ===

==== Kozo Togashi ====
{{nihongo|Togashi Kozo|渡越幸三}}, known professionally as "The Spear," hails from [[Yomitan]], [[Yanbaru]]. His background in traditional [[Ti]] martial arts translated seamlessly to professional wrestling, where his devastating spear tackle became his signature maneuver.

Togashi spent twelve years in NOPW, holding the [[IGO Intercontinental Championship]] twice before returning to Yanbaru to establish the '''Pacific Wrestling Alliance''' in 2015.

==== The Coconut Brothers ====
Born {{nihongo|Tamura Hiroshi|田村浩}} and {{nihongo|Tamura Kenji|田村健}}, The Coconut Brothers ({{nihongo|椰子兄弟|Yashi Kyohdai}}) originated from the [[Agarihama]] district of Yanbaru. Their high-energy tag team style incorporates dance breaks, crowd participation, and their signature '''Coconut Crush''', a modified double-team powerslam.

The brothers achieved significant success in NOPW, holding the [[IGO Tag Team Championship]] three times before retiring in 2019 to operate a wrestling school in their hometown.

=== Nakamian wrestling stars ===

==== Kawada Masahiro ====
From the historic city of [[Miyagami]] in southern [[Nakamizu]], {{nihongo|Kawada Masahiro|河田正浩}} represents the pinnacle of Nakamian Strong-Technico style. His brutal striking combined with elite submission skills made his matches against Honda Tadakatsu legendary encounters.

Kawada's '''Stretch Plum''' submission hold and '''Dangerous Brainbuster''' are considered among the most devastating moves in wrestling.

==== Takagi Yuto ====
{{nihongo|Takagi Yuto|鷹木勇人}}, known as "The Dragon," combines raw power with surprising agility. The Nakamian star's {{nihongo|Made in Nakamizu}} pumping lariat has become his calling card. Takagi currently competes in both NOPW and the [[Kawaei Shogunate Wrestling]] promotion in Nakamizu.

== Relations with professional wrestling abroad ==

=== Foreigners in Sanese circuits ===
Okaiken has a long history of incorporating foreign wrestlers, known as ''gaijin'', to challenge native talent. Since the 1950s, these performers—primarily from [[Lurandia]], [[Mercia]], and [[Vaiahi]]—have been utilized as "invading villains" or respected rivals to help build the prestige of Sanese champions.

In recent decades, stars from [[Lurandia]] such as [[Danny Viggo|El Phantasma]] have found immense success in the junior heavyweight division. The introduction of [[lucha libre]] from [[Volisania]] and southern Abyalan circuits led to the development of "Lucha-Puro," a high-flying style exemplified by the second and third generations of the [[Tiger Mask]] lineage.

