=== Sanese stars abroad ===
Promotions like NOPW have a long-standing tradition of sending young wrestlers on "Excursion" to [[Lurandia]], [[Volisania]], and the [[United Provinces]] to learn diverse styles. Famous examples include [[Hayabusa]]'s legendary run in Volisanian lucha circuits and [[Tiger Mask (IV)|Tiger Mask IV]]'s appearances in the Abyalan Cruiserweight championships.

Notable excursions include:
* '''[[Ryohei Maeda]]''': Spent two years in Lurandia, developing the "Speed Star" persona
* '''[[Honda Masanori]]''': Trained in [[Andalus]] before returning to found AOPW
* '''[[KAZUKI]]''': Currently on excursion in [[Lurandia]] wrestling circuits
* '''[[Tanahashi Hiroshi]]''': Veteran excursion to Volisania in 2006

Sanese wrestlers often adopt new personae abroad; many sent to Volisania adopt the mask, while those in Lurandia frequently play into the "Mystic East" or "Technocratic Mastermind" tropes. In the 2020s, stars like [[Nakamura Shinsuke]] and [[Asuka (wrestler)|Asuka]] have become household names in Illypnia, with the former maintaining his "Strong Style" identity while performing for major Lurandian networks.

=== Vaiahi connections ===
The [[Vaiahi]] Islands share a unique relationship with Okaiken wrestling. The large Vaiahi population in the [[Yonezawa Prefecture|Yonezawa]] and [[Tokuyama Prefecture|Tokuyama]] regions has created a natural pipeline for talent exchange. The '''Anoa'i-Masua''' wrestling family maintains training facilities in both Vaiahi and Okaiken.

NOPW's annual '''Island Invasion Tour''' travels throughout Vaiahi, Yanbaru, and Nakamizu, drawing massive crowds and strengthening interarchipelago wrestling relations. The tour culminates in the '''Shendan Cup''', a tournament featuring wrestlers from all three Sanese nations.

